Tou -> 25
Val -> 1
Wiz -> 1
       ---
       269 games

5% ascension rate, 15% for non-Arc
I really seem to suck at Arc :-(
Had 2 times a sequence of 3 back-to-back ascensions.
One game was very easy due to a level 1 wand of wishing (Healer).
I noticed altars seem to be much more likely than they used to be,
never needed to convert the mine-town altar, which I used to do quite
often.
Spell based playing seems to work better now.
Never got any wishes from potions.
Blew up my ascension kit three times by putting wand of cancellation in my
bag of holding. Ascended all of them anyways (but only because I wanted to
finish this sequence. In plain games I'll just quit if this happens again,
just too annoying (in fact I now simply leave wands of cancellation behind
in the late game)).
No conducts, not really my style. Ate whatever I liked as monk and killed
lots of peacefuls as knight. Polylined, genocided and wished like there was
no tomorrow.
The riders seem a lot easier than I remember them. Were they downgraded ?
Saw two woodchucks, which I had never met before (I know, never generated
normally, but I never saw them before. Are they recent ?)
One of the woodchucks actually was on the oracle level and walked up to her.
Nothing happened, which was disappointing.
Alchemy makes the end much easier than it used to be. Also much faster.
Overall I think the shortening of the end is good. I don't bother with
nurse dancing anymore after a basically won char was caught naked by a heavy
hitter.
I went through levels much quicker than I used to, and often arrived at
Medusa with a very sparse inventory, quite often missing levitation.

Most common death cause: killed by a sewer rat (13 times, how embarrassing)
